Amendment. Section 1 of EO No. 208, as amended, is hereby
further amended to read as follows:
"Section 1. Composition of the Commission. The PCW shall
be composed of the following members:
THE PRESIDENT OF THE PHILIPPINES

1.1
A Chairperson who shall be appointed by the President and
shall serve on a full-time basis with the rank and
emoluments of an Undersecretary;
1.2
Heads of the following government agencies who shall sit in the
Commission as ex-officio members:
1.2.1 Department of Agriculture;
1.2.2 Department of Budget and Management;
1.2.3
Department of Education;
1.2.4
Department of Foreign Affairs;
1.2.5 Department of Health;
1.2.6
Department of the Interior and Local Government;
1.2.7 Department of Labor and Employment;
1.2.8 Department of Social Welfare and Development;
1.2.9 Department of Trade and Industry; and
1.2.10 National Economic and Development Authority;
1.3
Twelve (12) members from civil society representing the
following sectors:
1.3.2 Business and Industry;
1.3.3 Science and Health;
1.3.4 Education or Academe;
1.3.6 Indigenous Peoples;
1.3.7 Farmers and Fisherfolks;
1.3.8 Senior Citizens;
1.3.9 Persons with Disabilities;
1.3.10 Media, Culture and the Arts;
1.3.12 One (1) representative of the National Council of Women in the
Philippines.
The incumbent members of the Commission, however, shall
continue to hold office unless replaced or removed by the President.
The heads of government agencies mentioned are
authorized to designate their permanent alternates with a rank not
lower than Assistant Secretary to represent them during
Commission meetings and other official functions. The ex-officio
member shall inform the Commission in writing of such
designation.
There is hereby created a PCW Secretariat, which shall be
headed by an Executive Director, and assisted by two (2) Deputy
Executive Directors, who shall, among other functions, supervise
the provision of requisite technical and administrative services to
the members of the Commission.'
